10c7|a|The act of impelling, or driving onward with sudden force; impulsion; especially, force so communicated as to produced motion suddenly, or immediately. ; The effect of an impelling force; motion produced by a sudden or momentary force. ; The action of a force during a very small interval of time; the effect of such action; as, the impulse of a sudden blow upon a hard elastic body. ; A mental force which simply and directly urges to action; hasty inclination; sudden motive; momentary or transient influence of appetite or passion; propension; incitement; as, a man of good impulses; passion often gives a violent impulse to the will.	j:g8a,97,2;eme,93,6;g8c,83,4;239s,45,2;21tb,42,5;24au,40,1;1py8,39,6;9v5,37,4;tau,34,3;1cp0,34,3;s81,18,3;bu1,8,4;1kqj,6,4;fdl,4,2~eme,93,6;1py8,39,6;21tb,42,5;1kqj,6,4;bu1,8,4;g8c,83,4;9v5,37,4;s81,18,3;1cp0,34,3;tau,34,3;239s,45,2;g8a,97,2;fdl,4,2;24au,40,1
